{
  "ai": {
    "chunks": [
      "Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. 'Ali b. al-Husayn b. Musa b. Babawayh al-Qummi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us. He said: Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. Ishaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us. He said: Abu Sa'id al-Hasan b. 'Ali al-'Adawi narrated to us. He said: Yusuf b. Yahya al-Isfahani Abu Ya'qub narrated to us. He said: Abu 'Ali Isma'il b. Hatim narrated to me. He said: Abu Ja'far Ahmad b. Salih b. Sa'id al-Makki narrated to us. He said: 'Amr b. Hafs narrated to us from Ishaq b. Najih from Khusayf from Mujahid from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) gave a wasiyya (will) to Ali b. Abi Talib (peace be upon him) and said:",
      "O Ali! When the bride is brought to your house, remove her shoes when she sits and wash her feet, then pour the water at the farthest edge of your dwelling, for if you do so, Allah will remove seventy thousand types of poverty from your house and send down seventy thousand types of blessing and bestow seventy thousand mercies upon the bride. O Ali! Beware of intercourse on the first, the middle, and the last of the month, for verily insanity, leprosy, and mental decline come upon the child. O Ali! Do not speak during intercourse, for if a child is conceived, it may be mute. Let none of you look at the private parts of his wife, and lower your gazes. O Ali! Do not have intercourse with your wife while desiring another woman, for I fear that if a child is destined, it would be an effeminate man or a masculine woman.",
      "O Ali! Do not have intercourse with your wife in the state of menstruation, for if a child is destined, it will be leprous. O Ali! Do not have intercourse with your wife after the midday prayer, for if a child is destined, it will be cross-eyed. O Ali! Do not speak during intercourse and do not be hasty. O Ali! Do not have intercourse with your wife under a fruit tree, for the child may be an executioner. O Ali! Do not have intercourse on the rooftop, for if a child is destined, it will be a hypocrite. O Ali! If your wife is pregnant, do not have intercourse without ablution. O Ali! Do not have intercourse with your wife on the night of Eid al-Fitr, for the child may be evil. O Ali! Do not have intercourse on the night of Eid al-Adha. O Ali! Do not have intercourse under the open sky.",
      "O Ali! Do not have intercourse facing the qibla. O Ali! Do not have intercourse in a boat. O Ali! Do not sit at the table of people who drink wine. O Ali! Do not enter the bathhouse without an izar. O Ali! Do not wear a ring of brass. O Ali! Do not perform ablution in a place where you have bathed from impurity. O Ali! Do not borrow from your neighbor's cooking pot unless you know its contents. O Ali! Do not refuse perfume, for it is light to carry and pleasant in scent. O Ali! Make sure to use the siwak, for the siwak purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord.",
      "O Ali! Recite Ayat al-Kursi at the time of every prayer, for you will be under the protection of Allah. O Ali! Recite Surah Yasin, for it contains ten blessings. O Ali! Beware of lying, for lying darkens the face. O Ali! Do not envy, for envy consumes good deeds as fire consumes wood. O Ali! Beware of anger, for the beginning of anger is madness and its end is regret. O Ali! Beware of excessive eating, for it hardens the heart. O Ali! Give charity in the early morning, for calamity does not pass charity. O Ali! Preserve this wasiyya of mine as I preserved it from Jibril."
    ],
